Sickbed substations are patient-facing communication devices integrated into hospital nurse-call systems. These devices allow patients to request assistance, communicate with nursing personnel, and access selected bedside control functions.
The market is developing as hospitals modernize inpatient wards, intensive care units, geriatric care facilities, and specialized clinical environments. Increasing emphasis on patient safety, healthcare service efficiency, and effective communication between patients and medical personnel is supporting demand for advanced bedside communication terminals.
Modern sickbed substations may incorporate physical call buttons, handsets, integrated communication panels, touch-control interfaces, and network-connected intercom functions.
